  abstract={This article presents a line-connected Q-sampler-based (LQS) multi-phase (MP) hybrid converter for direct conversion from high-rail to point-of-load (PoL). The proposed topology uses an input-parallel switched-capacitor (SC) structure to support “ALL-ON” operation during load transients, while a “multi-source- ${V}_{\mathrm { X}}$ ” control decouples voltage conversion ratio (VCR) from phase count, enabling a wide VCR range and all-phase interleaving. In addition, the line-connected structure preserves phase scalability, while the Q-samplers provide inherent inductor current  ${I}_{\mathrm { L}}$  balancing. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first reported MP hybrid converter that achieves these features simultaneously. The zero-DC-voltage property of the Q-sample capacitors minimizes area overhead. The proposed LQS approach is also extendable to other hybrid topologies. Fabricated in a 0.18- $\mu $ m bipolar-CMOS-DMOS (BCD) process, the prototype six-phase converter delivers up to 8-A load current with 91.5% peak efficiency and a 1.8% maximum inductor current imbalance ratio. With “ALL-ON” control enabled during transients, the converter achieves a normalized output undershoot (US) ratio of 0.41.},
